  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict transformation, food security and sustainable development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary focus of Kdadalak Sulimutuk Institut (KSI) is peace-building and conflict transformation, which necessarily links in with helping grassroots communities find constructive ways to solve practical problems.  The objective of this project is to help rural communities in Ermera and Manufahi Districts to improve and consolidate their food security (which necessarily includes land rights), and to raise household incomes.  The approach is based on the findings of an intensive participatory consultation process carried out with the communities prior to the start of the present cycle of CAFOD funding in 2011.  Workshops are held to validate those findings and produce Community Action Plans.  Practical support and training are provided, and demonstration plots established, to promote crop diversification and new or enhanced skills in agriculture and animal husbandry.  Efforts to increase production go in tandem with analysis and strategic planning for improved access to markets, formation and consolidation of co-operatives, disaster risk reduction, environmental conservation and appropriate technology. The socio-economic components are integrated into a process of community empowerment and conflict transformation, and capacity-building activities are undertaken to help beneficiaries develop a more active and informed citizenship, engage in public discussion of issues affecting their lives, and network constructively with decision-makers, media, and other partners.  A key tool for improvement of social cohesion is the documentation and creative use of traditional culture.</narrative>
  </description>
